// EXEMPLAR — settings.gradle of a hexagonal multi-module project (Gradle, Groovy DSL).
// Compilable as-is once the module list matches the blueprint. DO NOT invent module
// names: mirror `modules[]` from the active blueprint, same discipline as
// pom.parent.xml.example's <modules> block.
//
// Gradle has no per-module POM to declare the graph in — this file is the one place the
// module list lives. A colon path (`adapters:adapter-in-rest`) maps to the folder
// `adapters/adapter-in-rest` automatically; no `project(':...').projectDir` override
// needed as long as the folder structure matches.
//
// Unlike the Maven <modules> block, declaration order here carries no meaning — Gradle
// resolves the build graph from each module's own `project(':...')` dependency
// declarations in its build.gradle, not from this list's order.
rootProject.name = 'minha-api'

include 'domain'
include 'application'
include 'adapters:adapter-in-rest'
include 'adapters:adapter-out-persistence'
include 'bootstrap'

// layout: single-module never gets this file beyond the `rootProject.name` line above —
// there is nothing to include, the Initializr's own build.gradle already is the whole
// project. Don't add an `include` block in that case.
